# Mpumalanga Schools Closed Due to Severe Weather Conditions

JOHANNESBURG - The Mpumalanga Education Department has decided to halt classes at several schools until next Monday due to severe weather conditions.

In certain districts, principals have been advised to use their judgment to ensure safety. Authorities have advised against reopening schools unless it is deemed safe.

Educators and students have faced difficulties reaching schools because of swollen rivers and hazardous roads.

Since December, storms have claimed 19 lives in Mpumalanga and Limpopo. Both provinces have faced intense storms resulting in loss of life and widespread damage.

In Limpopo, the government has called upon areas affected by floods to take necessary precautions.

Severe weather patterns are anticipated to persist through the weekend.

Emergency and disaster response teams continue to maintain a heightened state of readiness.
