FAYETTEVILLE, Ark. — Weather forecasts predict temperatures ranging from the low 30s to the low 20s, accompanied by chilly winds on Saturday, Jan. 17. These anticipated overnight conditions have led Fayetteville to implement its extreme-weather protocol.

According to the city, the extreme-weather protocol ensures that community members have a secure, heated refuge available during periods of severe cold.

Individuals seeking overnight accommodation are advised to arrive at Potter's House located within Jefferson Elementary at 612 S. College Avenue by 5 p.m. Meals for both dinner and breakfast will be included.

Currently, the activation is scheduled solely for Saturday, Jan. 17, although the Fayetteville C.R.E.W. team remains vigilant, assessing weather conditions daily.

