With 2025 ranking as the third-most significant year for billion-dollar disasters on record, it is surpassed solely by 2023 and 2024. This year notably exceeds the established long-term norm of nine such occurrences annually, alongside an average yearly expense of $67.6 billion, according to records starting from 1980.

