According to their findings, more than forty years ago in June 1983, The Wexford People described Lady's Island Lake as "almost a cess pool" and stated that the recreational site was "being shamelessly destroyed by pollution."

The extremely unique habitat is now described as being on the verge of collapse amidst what is being dubbed an environmental disaster.
