On Wednesday, 24 September, super typhoon Ragasa, recognized as the most powerful tropical cyclone globally this year, struck southern China, resulting in fatalities and injuries. Its path of devastation also caused extensive destruction in the Philippines, Taiwan, and Hong Kong.

Originating in the western Pacific, this super typhoon intensified as it absorbed energy from the warming ocean waters before escalating to a category 5 typhoon—the peak classification on the Saffir–Simpson hurricane wind scale—featuring wind speeds of 260 km/h.

