A potential disaster on the Milan-Lecco railway was narrowly avoided on Wednesday as firefighters successfully halted a locomotive mere meters from a section of track compromised by a sinkhole. This dangerous situation was caused by severe storms sweeping across various regions of Italy since Tuesday.

The surge of severe weather has led to extensive destruction and upheaval, affecting numerous regions with floods, landslides, and toppled trees. Firefighters are overwhelmed as they attempt to manage a surge in emergency calls. Approximately 200 individuals found themselves isolated on the island of Elba when a landslide blocked a road near Forno beach.

